#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:80
msgid "2 Creating the structure to hold launch files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:82
msgid ""
"By convention, all launch files for a package are stored in the ``launch`` "
"directory inside of the package. Make sure to create a ``launch`` directory "
"at the top-level of the package you created above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:89
msgid ""
"For Python packages, the directory containing your package should look like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:91
msgid ""
"src/\n"
"  py_launch_example/\n"
"    launch/\n"
"    package.xml\n"
"    py_launch_example/\n"
"    resource/\n"
"    setup.cfg\n"
"    setup.py\n"
"    test/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:103
msgid ""
"To enable colcon to locate and utilize our launch files, we need to inform "
"Python's setup tools of their presence. To achieve this, open the ``setup."
"py`` file, add the necessary ``import`` statements at the top, and include "
"the launch files into the ``data_files`` parameter of ``setup``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:106
msgid ""
"import os\n"
"from glob import glob\n"
"# Other imports ...\n"
"\n"
"package_name = 'py_launch_example'\n"
"\n"
"setup(\n"
"    # Other parameters ...\n"
"    data_files=[\n"
"        # ... Other data files\n"
"        # Include all launch files.\n"
"        (os.path.join('share', package_name, 'launch'), glob('launch/*'))\n"
"    ]\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:125
msgid ""
"For C++ packages, we will only be adjusting the ``CMakeLists.txt`` file by "
"adding:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:127
msgid ""
"# Install launch files.\n"
"install(DIRECTORY\n"
"  launch\n"
"  DESTINATION share/${PROJECT_NAME}/\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:135
msgid "to the end of the file (but before ``ament_package()``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:139
msgid "3 Writing the launch file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:143
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:188
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:210
msgid "XML launch file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:145
msgid ""
"Inside your ``launch`` directory, create a new launch file called "
"``my_script_launch.xml``. ``_launch.xml`` is recommended, but not required, "
"as the file suffix for XML launch files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:148
msgid ""
"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n"
"<launch>\n"
"  <node pkg=\"demo_nodes_cpp\" exec=\"talker\" name=\"talker\"/>\n"
"</launch>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:151
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:194
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:216
msgid "YAML launch file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:153
msgid ""
"Inside your ``launch`` directory, create a new launch file called "
"``my_script_launch.yaml``. ``_launch.yaml`` is recommended, but not "
"required, as the file suffix for YAML launch files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:156
msgid ""
"%YAML 1.2\n"
"---\n"
"launch:\n"
"  - node:\n"
"      pkg: \"demo_nodes_cpp\"\n"
"      exec: \"talker\"\n"
"      name: \"talker\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:159
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:200
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:222
msgid "Python launch file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:161
msgid ""
"Inside your ``launch`` directory, create a new launch file called "
"``my_script_launch.py``. ``_launch.py`` is recommended, but not required, as "
"the file suffix for Python launch files. However, the launch file name needs "
"to end with ``launch.py`` to be recognized and autocompleted by ``ros2 "
"launch``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:165
msgid ""
"Your launch file should define the ``generate_launch_description()`` "
"function which returns a ``launch.LaunchDescription()`` to be used by the "
"``ros2 launch`` verb."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Launch-system.rst:167
msgid ""
"import launch\n"
"import launch_ros.actions\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"    return launch.LaunchDescription([\n"
"        launch_ros.actions.Node(\n"
"            package='demo_nodes_cpp',\n"
"            executable='talker',\n"
"            name='talker'),\n"
"    ])\n"
msgstr ""

